## Context

Commit edda724b moved raw model replies from `experiments/outputs/<dir>/`
to `experiments/archive/outputs/<dir>/`, leaving only `.record.json`
pointers in the live dirs. Render/score rules that read raw replies from
the live dirs via `$(wildcard ...)` now expand to EMPTY prerequisite
lists and produce empty or failing output — the exact failure pattern
0417 fixed for `tab_source_grounding.tex`, on other files.

Confirmed by running the producers (2026-06-04, during 0417):

- `tabulate_coherence --input experiments/outputs/rag_extract` →
  "No extractions found — table will be empty. Wrote ... (0 models)".
  `outputs/rag_extract/` has 0 CSVs live; 39 in archive.
  (`ANALYSIS_RAG_CSVS`, render.mk:77 + recipe render.mk:316)
- `tabulate_decomposition_fix` → "No reconciliation CSVs found in
  either directory". `outputs/rag_per_fuel{,_v2}/` are record-only.
  (`ANALYSIS_DECOMP_BEFORE/AFTER`, render.mk:75-76)
- Suspect, not yet confirmed: `SCORE_SC_INPUT := $(SCORE_OUTPUTS)/rag`
  (score.mk:156) — `experiments/outputs/rag/` does not exist at all
  (neither does `archive/outputs/rag/`); check what the
  self-consistency scorer actually needs.

NOT affected (verified): `exp1_batch2/` (140 data files live),
`sota_exp3_arm*_batch1/` (data in `run*/` subdirs, untouched).

The committed tables (`tab_coherence.tex`, `tab_decomposition_fix.tex`)
are still the correct pre-move content — the breakage is latent: any
rebuild would silently REPLACE them with empty tables (0383 hazard).
The 0417 guard does not catch this: it checks rule existence, not rule
correctness.

## Actions

1. Sweep every `$(wildcard ...)` / `--input` over `experiments/outputs/`
   in render.mk and score.mk; classify each dir live-data vs record-only.
2. Repoint broken readers to `experiments/archive/outputs/` (tracked P1
   outcomes per 0405), following the 0417 pattern
   (`tabulate_source_grounding`: script constant + rule prereqs).
3. Apply the 0383 gate per fix: regenerate, require byte-identical
   output before committing; any diff stops for review.
4. Consider a guard: a rule whose raw-reply wildcard expands empty
   while the matching archive dir is non-empty is a red flag
   (adherence test or build-time assertion).

## Verification

- [x] tab_coherence repointed to archive; regenerated byte-identical (15 models)
- [x] self-consistency scorer repointed (doubly stale: rag→rag_extract→archive);
      NOT byte-verified (rule writes measurements.jsonl — 0383 hazard)
- [x] tab_decomposition_fix FROZEN — reconciliation CSVs gitignored, never
      archived; rule removed, added to FROZEN_ALLOWLIST with documented reason
- [x] Script defaults + docstrings updated (coherence, self_consistency,
      decomposition_fix)
- [x] make check-fast green; DAG guard green; score-build-no-acquire green

## Exit criteria

- [x] Every render/score rule reading raw replies resolves to non-empty
      inputs (or is retired/frozen with evidence)
- [x] Regenerated tables byte-identical to committed ones (0383) where safe
      to run; frozen with reason where not
- [ ] `make check` green
